  "summary": "Experience the luxurious side of classic French cooking with this fruit slow braise that is <b>finished as an elegant dessert</b>. Firm Bosc pears are submerged in a fragrant braising liquid composed of full-bodied red wine, whole cinnamon sticks, star anise, orange peel, and dark cocoa powder. As the pot simmers slowly in a low oven, the pears absorb deep crimson hues and floral spice essences while softening into buttery tenderness. The braising liquor is reduced into a glossy, bittersweet chocolate sauce that coats each glistening pear with silky indulgence. Served warm alongside a dollop of cold crème fraîche, this dessert combines deep red wine tannins with dark chocolate richness for an unforgettable conclusion to a dinner party. Braising whole peeled pears low and slow preserves their elegant stem structure while infusing flavors directly into the core of the fruit.",
